    ✗ L14: client = mqtt.Client(client_id=cfg.client_id)  — amqtt has no class named 'Client' with this constructor signature. The equivalen
  ⚠ Remaining incompatibilities noted by connector LLM:
    - amqtt's MQTTClient API is exclusively async (async connect(), async publish(), requires an asyncio event loop); paho-mqtt's Client is synchronous and 
callback-based. Bridging this at just the constructor call site is insufficient — publish_reading() and publish_batch() are synchronous methods returning plain
dicts/lists to callers, so any wrapper that forces async calls into a sync-looking API must block on an event loop for every publish, which changes 
concurrency/latency behavior and cannot be considered a faithful drop-in replacement.
    - amqtt's publish() does not return an object with an 'rc' return-code attribute analogous to paho-mqtt's MQTTMessageInfo; the whole rc-based result 
contract used in publish_reading() has no direct semantic equivalent, requiring behavioral guesswork rather than a straightforward wrapper.
    - amqtt is a QoS/session-feature-limited, less-actively-maintained implementation per the stated pitfalls, so full feature parity (e.g. reconnect handling,
persistent session, TLS options used implicitly via paho.Client kwargs) cannot be guaranteed even with wrapper glue code.

